That might help a little, but honestly, you can dig a path across the
maze portion once and then walk straight across for the rest of the
game -- but you still have to walk from the up stairs clear at the
west end all the way to the one and only entrance to the core lair
way down near the east end, then thread your way back through the
core lair to the down stairs near the west end thereof.  (That's
Asmo's lair.  Baalzebub's is laid out differently but is almost as
bad in terms of making you go far out of your way.)  If you're on
your way up, it's the same in reverse.  (Actually, on the way up
is the main issue, because on the way down you can dig a hole.)
If only the core lair were non-teleport, you could teleport to
the entrance end of it, but then you've still got to walk clear
through the core lair.  Baalzebub's is more or less a spiral.  It
seems specifically designed to wear out your character's shoes.

